    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0249" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/1036: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting Chairman of the American Delegation (Gibson)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-16T16:00:00-04:00">May 16, 1932—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. Special for Gibson and Davis. Your 169, May 13, 4 p.m., from
                    London.</p>
                <p>When Mr. Baldwin made suggestion as to
                    capital ships contained in your Section 4, did either of you inform him (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) as to the position taken by the American
                    Delegation at London in 1930,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d84-f1"/> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) as to my recent statements on the subject in
                    Geneva or (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) as to the functions capital ships are
                    now performing in respect to the Far East? Please immediately send full details
                    and his reply if any.</p>
                <p>Did you gather that Mr. Baldwin’s failure
                    to include submarines in his list of weapons to be abolished was an over-sight
                    or intentional; if intentional, did he give any explanation therefor?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d84-f1" n="11" xml:id="d84-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 35, February 4, from the Chairman of the American delegation,
                        <ref target="frus1930v01#pg_13">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1930, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 13</ref>; and telegram No. 212, April
                    10, from the Chairman of the American delegation, <ref
                        target="frus1930v01#pg_106">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 106</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
